Aether: Glean DOM bindings and docs out

Glean WebIDL bindings and metric layer, telemetry docs trees, extension Glean global.

Squashed from 3 units:

  [core/102-no-glean-dom-bindings.patch]
  Aether: remove the Glean DOM bindings and stale telemetry docs
  
  Remove the Glean DOM API (the three Glean WebIDL files and their window attributes, the Bindings.conf block including the nsIGleanPing iface, the nsGlobalWindowInner accessors, and the DOM-only C++ classes) plus the entire C++ metric-type layer that only served it and the FOG gtest (private/*, GleanMetric, MetricTypes, the generated JS lookups, the GleanPing impl, TestFog, the legacy telemetry event/histogram/scalar gtests, and the dead GPU test-metrics include) and the empty ReportBrokenSite recorder. Also drop the stale telemetry docs (the obsolete collection and the install-ping page). What stays: the standalone no-op metric declarations for the JS engine, the JOG factory, FOG IPC, the codegen rules, and the Rust SDK with its neutered uploader.\n
  
  [core/103-no-telemetry-docs.patch]
  Aether: remove the telemetry and Glean doc trees
  
  Remove the two doc trees that only document removed systems (Desktop Telemetry and FOG/Glean instrumentation) along with their sphinx registrations and lint exclusions. Docs never ship in the product; this is tree hygiene so no prose describes systems that no longer exist.\n
  
  [core/104-no-extension-glean-global.patch]
  Aether: drop the dead Glean globals from the extension sandbox
  
  Remove the Glean and GleanPings globals injected into every extension sandbox: the JS API behind them is gone, so each sandbox creation threw a ReferenceError. Nothing could consume them.\n
